hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"958","[958] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar: He used to say In this regard, such as the saying of Aisha, may God be pleased with her - Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 958 Arabic Hadith:"
"1090","[1090] Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Rifa’i Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Zubayr: During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Rifa’a bin Samwal divorced his wife, Tamimah bint Wahb, three times, so she married Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Zubair, so he turned away from her and was not able to touch her, so he separated from her, and Rifa’a wanted to marry her, and he was her husband. The first was the one who divorced her, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he forbade him from marrying her and said: It is not permissible for you until Taste the honey. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1090 Arabic Hadith:"
"1859","He told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that he heard him say that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lowered his forelock as God wished, and then They separated after that. Malik said, “There is nothing wrong with a man looking at the hair of his son’s wife or the hair of his wife’s mother.”"
"1860","He told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, that he hated castration and believed that creation was perfect in it."
"1861","He told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, that he had heard that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I and the one who takes care of an orphan for him or for someone else” Paradise is like these two if he fears “”””” He pointed with his middle finger and the one next to the thumb."
